<title>UK: No news seen on Ford/union talks till Friday.</title>
<headline>No news seen on Ford/union talks till Friday.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>British carmaking unions said on Thursday they are not expecting any announcement to come out of the first day of two-day talks with Ford Motor Co on the planned 1,300 job cuts at the Halewood plant in Liverpool.</p>
<p>Union negotiators met with Jac Nasser, chairman of the Ford European division in a bid to try and save the Halewood jobs.</p>
<p>The U.S. car giant is to axe around one third of the jobs at the plant after deciding to build the new model of the Ford Escort car on the Continent instead.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for the Transport and General Workers Union said an announcement on the talks is not expected until Friday afternoon.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 5427717</p>
